  "result": "Fixed: `--help` now lists an option's short name before its long name (`-v, --verbose`), where it previously showed `--verbose, -v`.\n\nThe cause was in `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py`: it sorted option names by prefix length in descending order. I removed the `reverse=True`, so shorter prefixes come first.\n\nI added `test_join_options_short_before_long` to `tests/test_formatting.py`. The full suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nI took \"weird order\" to mean the name order inside each option's entry. If you meant the order of the options themselves down the page, tell me and I'll look at `get_params`.\n\nI didn't touch `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`.",
